# Session projection cursor implementation contract — 2026-07-17

## Scope and boundary

Implement in `/private/tmp/ocean-os-session-projection-20260717` on `origin/main` `d87d7d9`. This is a content-bearing, session-scoped attach protocol for first-party transcript surfaces. It is separate from the accepted metadata-only Observatory program. Do not edit Observatory specs/code or route transcript/thinking/tool/permission content into Observatory.

Approved semantics:

- completed thinking is durable session snapshot content;
- in-progress thinking is transient projection state and resets across daemon epoch;
- `SurfacePatch` remains on its independent client-ledger lane and never advances this cursor;
- old clients/routes remain unchanged and best-effort;
- global content journal target is configurable, default 256 MiB;
- attach/reconnect leases are 60 seconds;
- committed checkpoints compact safely;
- malformed, wrong-session, wrong-epoch, future, evicted, or unretained cursors reset explicitly, never silently attach live;
- no staging or commits.

## Required correctness model

Let session JSON persistence remain the canonical durable provider history. Add a daemon-owned SQLite/WAL projection journal at `<config>/session-projection.db` (override `OCEAN_SESSION_PROJECTION_DB_PATH`). It stores ordered, session-scoped product frames and atomically folded ephemeral state. Broadcast is a wake hint only.

Each session has contiguous sequence numbers for retained projection frames. Internal persistence checkpoints do not consume a visible sequence. A snapshot returns:

1. the ordinary `SessionDetail` read from one atomic session JSON version;
2. a projection cursor at the latest journal sequence;
3. every retained agent/control frame strictly after the durable checkpoint sequence and through that cursor;
4. atomically folded state through the cursor: active turn/terminal telemetry, pending permission envelopes, mounted component render envelopes, and browser-active state.

The snapshot is therefore equivalent to hydrating SessionDetail, applying `pending_events`, then installing folded non-history state. Tail after `projection.cursor` is exclusive.

The session JSON and journal checkpoint align by a monotonic persistence revision:

- add `persistence_revision: u64` to persisted `ocean_agent::session::Session` with serde default 0;
- every successful atomic save writes revision+1 and updates the caller only after rename succeeds;
- expose revision additively on `SessionDetail`;
- add an INTERNAL `AgentEvent::PersistenceCheckpoint { session_id, persistence_revision }` emitted only after each successful accepted-user, provider-valid round, fake-provider, and final save;
- do not send the old runtime `TurnCheckpoint` to the daemon before persistence;
- daemon checkpoint handling records `checkpoint_revision` and sets `checkpoint_seq` to the latest visible sequence already committed for that session;
- on attach: file revision == journal revision is aligned; file newer with no active/in-flight state may be adopted atomically; journal newer causes bounded reread/retry; never return a cursor claiming a different file revision.

No filesystem I/O, registry lock, or `.await` may occur while holding the projection SQLite mutex.

## Additive wire contract

Add optional `projection` to existing `GET /v1/sessions/{id}` response; legacy clients ignore it. Recommended v1 shape:

```json
{
  "ok": true,
  "session": { "...": "existing SessionDetail", "persistence_revision": 17 },
  "projection": {
    "version": 1,
    "cursor": "sp1:<daemon-epoch>:<session-hash>:<seq>",
    "checkpoint_revision": 17,
    "pending_events": [
      {
        "cursor": "sp1:...",
        "source": "agent",
        "event": { "type": "assistant_text_delta", "...": "existing AgentTurnEvent JSON" }
      }
    ],
    "state": {
      "active_turn": null,
      "last_turn_finished": null,
      "pending_permissions": [],
      "components": [],
      "browser_active": false
    }
  }
}
```

Core protocol types may use `serde_json::Value` for event payloads to avoid circular crate dependencies, but cursor/source/state fields must be typed and tested.

Add `GET /v1/agent/projection/events?session_id=<id>&after_cursor=<cursor>`:

- `after_cursor` exclusive and required;
- subscribe to the projection wake bus before paging SQLite;
- page committed rows ascending, then wait for hints;
- broadcast lag re-pages SQLite;
- SSE `id:` is the projection cursor;
- SSE `data:` is the projection frame;
- keepalive and daemon shutdown behavior match existing agent SSE;
- any cursor parse/session/epoch/generation/retention problem sends one `event: projection_reset` with a closed reason and closes;
- never fall through to live after an unknown/evicted cursor.

Legacy `/v1/agent/events` UUID semantics and `/v1/events` remain wire-compatible.

## Journal/store requirements

Implement `crates/ocean-daemon/src/session_projection.rs` with unit tests.

Suggested SQLite schema:

- metadata/current daemon epoch;
- per `(epoch, session_id)` state: next/latest seq, checkpoint seq/revision, folded state JSON;
- append-only event rows keyed by `(epoch, session_id, seq)` with source, event JSON, exact serialized bytes, timestamp.

A daemon restart mints a new epoch and begins new per-session sequences; old cursors explicitly reset. Prior rows may remain until budget compaction, but are never replayed across epochs. Completed transcript/thinking reloads from session JSON; transient state starts empty.

Central producer coverage:

- attach the store to production `AgentEventBus`, appending before projection wake publication; keep its legacy in-memory UUID ring unchanged;
- include session-scoped `TurnStarted`, `ModelRerouted`, assistant/thinking deltas, tool start/chunk/finish, `TurnFinished`, `SessionCreated`, `ComponentRender`/Unmount, and `BrowserActivity`;
- explicitly exclude `SurfacePatch`, `SlackCanvas`, and generic `Extension` from the content journal (non-replayable or separate authority);
- attach the same store to legacy `EventBus` only for genuine `PermissionRequest`/`PermissionDecision` envelopes (skip `origin: agent` mirrors); fold pending permission state by permission_id;
- handle internal `PersistenceCheckpoint` directly through the bus/store checkpoint seam;
- append transaction updates event row, sequence, and folded state atomically; send wake only after commit;
- store errors mark the affected session reset-required and never claim continuity.

Compaction:

- default logical event JSON budget 256 MiB, env `OCEAN_SESSION_PROJECTION_JOURNAL_BYTES`;
- fixed 60-second lease, with test clock/config seam;
- normal compaction removes checkpoint-covered rows older than the lease horizon and not required by an active stream lease;
- pressure compaction removes oldest checkpoint-covered unprotected rows first;
- never delete events after a session checkpoint; temporary over-budget during a huge active round is preferable to silent loss;
- if continuity cannot be retained, mark/reset explicitly;
- snapshot and open tail establish/renew a lease; tail advances its protected minimum cursor as rows are sent; disconnect leaves protection until expiry.

## Fold semantics

- `TurnStarted`: set active turn.
- `TurnFinished`: clear active turn and retain terminal telemetry as `last_turn_finished`.
- `PermissionRequest`: upsert full safe legacy envelope by permission_id.
- `PermissionDecision`: remove by permission_id.
- `ComponentRender`: upsert current event by component_id.
- `ComponentUnmount`: remove component_id.
- `BrowserActivity`: set boolean.
- transcript/tool/thinking deltas remain ordered pending frames until subsumed by a committed checkpoint.
- `PersistenceCheckpoint`: advance checkpoint revision/seq; no visible seq.
- `SurfacePatch`: no seq/budget/state change.

## Tests and docs

Required focused tests:

- legacy session JSON revision 0; first save 1; same-ms saves distinct; failed save leaves memory/disk revision unchanged;
- checkpoints emitted only after successful persistence for accepted user, tool-round, fake, final;
- two sessions have isolated contiguous cursors;
- snapshot pending frames + tail equality across every snapshot/publish interleaving;
- permission pending/resolution, component replace/unmount, browser true/false, active/finished fold;
- SurfacePatch does not move cursor or bytes;
- wrong session/epoch, malformed/future/evicted cursors reset;
- wake subscribe-before-page and lag catch-up;
- lease renewal/expiry and checkpoint compaction;
- restart epoch reset with completed transcript retained and transient thinking cleared;
- no Observatory files/types/routes touched.

Update nearest `AGENTS.md`, `crates/AGENTS.md` only if shared contract text changes, current architecture/operations/project-map docs as necessary, and append root `events.md` entry with the worktree path. Do not edit accepted Observatory specs.

Validation at minimum:

```sh
cargo test -p ocean-core
cargo test -p ocean-runtime
cargo test -p ocean-agent-sdk
cargo test -p ocean-agent session
cargo test -p ocean-agent
cargo test -p ocean-daemon session_projection -- --nocapture
cargo test -p ocean-daemon router_contract -- --nocapture
cargo test -p ocean-daemon permission_ -- --nocapture
cargo test -p ocean-daemon
cargo check --workspace --tests
cargo fmt --all -- --check
cargo clippy -p ocean-daemon --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo xtask docs-check
git diff --check
```

If this full contract cannot be completed safely in one pass, stop at a compile-clean, test-backed daemon checkpoint and clearly enumerate what is missing; do not ship or claim a UUID/buffering workaround as correct.

